IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgk-part9-declared`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 9 (Investigations), ss 243 to 246: inspectors who investigate the ownership of a company, the Minister's power to require information about the interests in shares or debentures,
-- restrictions on shares or debentures, and inspectors appointed in other countries.
-- The party and act types of the regulative rules are in sgk-part9-declared.l4.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The Minister, the inspectors and the Public Prosecutor appear only as what their acts mean to the person.
-- The Banking Act 1970 is not a source: what it provides enters as an input named for the fact.
-- Marks in the comments: "FALSE-kind" and "NOTHING-kind" say why a branch answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING; "fork F-Kn" points at the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `Section 243: inspectors to investigate the ownership of a company`

-- src:22409 | 243.—(1) Where it appears to the Minister that there is good reason
-- src:22410 | to do so, the Minister may appoint one or more inspectors to
-- src:22411 | investigate and report on the membership of any corporation, whether
-- src:22412 | or not it is a declared company, and otherwise with respect to the
-- src:22413 | corporation for the purpose of determining the true persons who are
-- src:22414 | or have been financially interested in the success or failure, real or
-- src:22415 | apparent, of the corporation or able to control or materially to
-- src:22416 | influence the policy of the corporation.
@ref s 243(1) (src:22409-22416)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister that there is good reason to appoint inspectors to investigate and report on the membership of the corporation and the true persons who are or have been financially interested in it or able to control or materially to influence its policy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(1) the Minister may appoint inspectors to investigate the ownership of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Minister that there is good reason to appoint inspectors to investigate and report on the membership of the corporation and the true persons who are or have been financially interested in it or able to control or materially to influence its policy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection begins "Where it appears to the Minister that there is good reason to do so"; a "may" gated by "where" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-K7)

-- src:22418 | (2) The appointment of an inspector under this section may define
-- src:22419 | the scope of the inspector’s investigation, whether as respects the
-- src:22420 | matters or the period to which it is to extend or otherwise, and in
-- src:22425 | particular may limit the investigation to matters connected with
-- src:22426 | particular shares or debentures.
@ref s 243(2) (src:22418-22426)
GIVEN `the appointment is an appointment of an inspector under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(2) the appointment may define the scope of the inspector's investigation` MEANS
    IF `the appointment is an appointment of an inspector under section 243`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "The appointment of an inspector under this section"

-- src:22428 | (3) Where an application for an investigation under this section
-- src:22429 | with respect to particular shares or debentures of a corporation is
-- src:22430 | made to the Minister by members of the corporation, and the number
-- src:22431 | of applicants or the amount of the shares held by them is not less than
-- src:22432 | that required for an application for the appointment of an inspector
-- src:22433 | under section 232, the Minister must appoint an inspector to conduct
-- src:22434 | the investigation unless the Minister is satisfied that the application is
-- src:22435 | vexatious, and the inspector’s appointment must not exclude from the
-- src:22436 | scope of the inspector’s investigation any matter which the
-- src:22437 | application seeks to have included therein, except insofar as the
-- src:22438 | Minister is satisfied that it is unreasonable for that matter to be
-- src:22439 | investigated.
@ref s 243(3) (src:22428-22439)
GIVEN `an application for an investigation under section 243 with respect to particular shares or debentures of a corporation is made to the Minister by members of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of applicants or the amount of the shares held by them is not less than that required for an application for the appointment of an inspector under section 232` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the application is vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(3) the Minister must appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`an application for an investigation under section 243 with respect to particular shares or debentures of a corporation is made to the Minister by members of the corporation` AND `the number of applicants or the amount of the shares held by them is not less than that required for an application for the appointment of an inspector under section 232`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "Where an application ... is made to the Minister by members of the corporation, and the number of applicants or the amount of the shares held by them is not less than that required"; a "where" unmet on a duty (fork F-K5; the threshold is an input: fork F-K31)
    ELSE (IF `the Minister is satisfied that the application is vexatious`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Minister is satisfied that the application is vexatious"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 243(3) (src:22428-22439)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 243(3) the Minister must appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 the Minister`
    MUST `s 243(3) appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 243(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation the application sought" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

@ref s 243(3) (src:22428-22439)
GIVEN `an application for an investigation under section 243 with respect to particular shares or debentures of a corporation is made to the Minister by members of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of applicants or the amount of the shares held by them is not less than that required for an application for the appointment of an inspector under section 232` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application seeks to have the matter included in the scope of the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that it is unreasonable for the matter to be investigated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(3) the appointment must not exclude the matter from the scope of the investigation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`an application for an investigation under section 243 with respect to particular shares or debentures of a corporation is made to the Minister by members of the corporation` AND `the number of applicants or the amount of the shares held by them is not less than that required for an application for the appointment of an inspector under section 232` AND `the application seeks to have the matter included in the scope of the investigation`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the prohibition arises "Where an application ... is made ... the inspector's appointment must not exclude ... any matter which the application seeks to have included"; a "where" unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)
    ELSE (IF `the Minister is satisfied that it is unreasonable for the matter to be investigated`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except insofar as the Minister is satisfied that it is unreasonable for that matter to be investigated"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:22441 | (4) Subject to the terms of an inspector’s appointment, the
-- src:22442 | inspector’s powers extend to the investigation of any circumstances
-- src:22443 | suggesting the existence of an arrangement or understanding which,
-- src:22444 | though not legally binding, is or was observed or likely to be observed
-- src:22445 | in practice and which is relevant to the purposes of the inspector’s
-- src:22446 | investigation.
@ref s 243(4) (src:22441-22446)
GIVEN `the terms of the inspector's appointment exclude the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances suggest the existence of an arrangement or understanding which, though not legally binding, is or was observed or likely to be observed in practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangement or understanding is relevant to the purposes of the inspector's investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(4) the inspector's powers extend to the investigation of the circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the terms of the inspector's appointment exclude the circumstances`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to the terms of an inspector's appointment" (fork F-K32: "subject to" is read as "unless")
    ELSE (IF `the circumstances suggest the existence of an arrangement or understanding which, though not legally binding, is or was observed or likely to be observed in practice` AND `the arrangement or understanding is relevant to the purposes of the inspector's investigation`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the powers "extend to the investigation of any circumstances suggesting the existence of an arrangement or understanding ... relevant to the purposes of the inspector's investigation"; the subsection says nothing of other circumstances

-- src:22448 | (5) For the purposes of any investigation under this section, the
-- src:22449 | provisions of this Part with respect to the investigation of declared
-- src:22450 | companies apply with the necessary modifications of references to
-- src:22451 | the affairs of the corporation or to those of any other corporation, but
-- src:22452 | so that —
-- src:22454 | (a) this Part applies in relation to all persons who are or have
-- src:22455 | been, or whom the inspector has reasonable cause to
-- src:22456 | believe to be or to have been financially interested in the
-- src:22457 | success or failure or the apparent success or failure of the
-- src:22458 | corporation or any other corporation the membership of
-- src:22459 | which is investigated with that of the corporation, or able to
-- src:22460 | control or materially to influence the policy thereof,
-- src:22461 | including persons concerned only on behalf of others, as
-- src:22462 | they apply in relation to officers and agents of the
-- src:22463 | corporation or of the other corporation, as the case may
-- src:22464 | be; and
-- src:22469 | (b) the Minister is not bound to furnish the corporation or any
-- src:22470 | other person with a copy of any report by an inspector
-- src:22471 | appointed under this section or with a complete copy
-- src:22472 | thereof if the Minister is of opinion that there is good
-- src:22473 | reason for not divulging the contents of the report or of
-- src:22474 | parts thereof, but may, if the Minister thinks fit, cause to be
-- src:22475 | kept by the Registrar a copy of the report or (as the case
-- src:22476 | may be) the parts of the report, as respects which the
-- src:22477 | Minister is not of that opinion.
@ref s 243(5) (src:22448-22477)
GIVEN `the investigation is an investigation under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(5) the provisions of Part 9 on the investigation of declared companies apply to the investigation with the necessary modifications` MEANS
    IF `the investigation is an investigation under section 243`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of any investigation under this section"

@ref s 243(5)(a) (src:22454-22464)
GIVEN `the investigation is an investigation under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is or has been financially interested in the success or failure, or the apparent success or failure, of the corporation or of another corporation the membership of which is investigated with that of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is or has been able to control or materially to influence the policy of the corporation or of another corporation the membership of which is investigated with that of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspector has reasonable cause to believe that the person is or has been so financially interested or able to control or influence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(5)(a) Part 9 applies in relation to the person as it applies in relation to officers and agents of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the investigation is an investigation under section 243` AND (`the person is or has been financially interested in the success or failure, or the apparent success or failure, of the corporation or of another corporation the membership of which is investigated with that of the corporation` OR `the person is or has been able to control or materially to influence the policy of the corporation or of another corporation the membership of which is investigated with that of the corporation` OR `the inspector has reasonable cause to believe that the person is or has been so financially interested or able to control or influence`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- "including persons concerned only on behalf of others"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this Part applies in relation to all persons who are or have been, or whom the inspector has reasonable cause to believe to be or to have been" so interested or able; the paragraph says nothing of anyone else

@ref s 243(5)(b) (src:22469-22477)
GIVEN `the investigation is an investigation under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is of the opinion that there is good reason for not divulging the contents of the report or of parts of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(5)(b) the Minister is not bound to furnish the person with a copy of the report or with a complete copy of it` MEANS
    IF `the investigation is an investigation under section 243` AND `the Minister is of the opinion that there is good reason for not divulging the contents of the report or of parts of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Minister is not bound ... if the Minister is of opinion that there is good reason for not divulging"; an exemption with an "if" (not "only if") gate answers like the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork F-K33)

@ref s 243(5)(b) (src:22469-22477)
GIVEN `the investigation is an investigation under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is of the report or of the parts of it as respects which the Minister is not of the opinion that there is good reason for not divulging the contents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(5)(b) the Minister may cause a copy of the report or of the parts of it to be kept by the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the investigation is an investigation under section 243` AND `the Minister thinks fit` AND `the copy is of the report or of the parts of it as respects which the Minister is not of the opinion that there is good reason for not divulging the contents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Minister "may, if the Minister thinks fit, cause to be kept by the Registrar a copy of the report or (as the case may be) the parts of the report, as respects which the Minister is not of that opinion"; a "may" with an "if" (not "only if") gate: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork F-K18)

§ `Section 244: information as to persons interested in shares or debentures`

-- src:22482 | 244.—(1) Where it appears to the Minister that there is good reason
-- src:22483 | to investigate the ownership of any shares in or debentures of a
-- src:22484 | corporation and that it is unnecessary to appoint an inspector for the
-- src:22485 | purpose, the Minister may require any person whom the Minister has
-- src:22486 | reasonable cause to believe to have or to be able to obtain any
-- src:22487 | information as to the present and past interests in those shares or
-- src:22488 | debentures and the names and addresses of the persons interested and
-- src:22489 | of any persons who act or have acted on their behalf in relation to the
-- src:22490 | shares or debentures to give such information to the Minister.
@ref s 244(1) (src:22482-22490)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister that there is good reason to investigate the ownership of the shares in or debentures of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister that it is unnecessary to appoint an inspector for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has reasonable cause to believe that the person has or is able to obtain information as to the present and past interests in those shares or debentures and the names and addresses of the persons interested and of any persons who act or have acted on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(1) the Minister may require the person to give the information to the Minister` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Minister that there is good reason to investigate the ownership of the shares in or debentures of the corporation` AND `it appears to the Minister that it is unnecessary to appoint an inspector for the purpose` AND `the Minister has reasonable cause to believe that the person has or is able to obtain information as to the present and past interests in those shares or debentures and the names and addresses of the persons interested and of any persons who act or have acted on their behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection begins "Where it appears to the Minister that there is good reason ... and that it is unnecessary to appoint an inspector" and reaches "any person whom the Minister has reasonable cause to believe to have or to be able to obtain" the information; a "may" gated by "where" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-K7)

-- src:22492 | (2) For the purposes of this section, a person is deemed to have an
-- src:22493 | interest in a share or debenture if the person has any right to acquire or
-- src:22494 | dispose of the share or debenture or any interest therein or to vote in
-- src:22495 | respect thereof, or if the person’s consent is necessary for the exercise
-- src:22496 | of any of the rights of other persons interested therein, or if other
-- src:22497 | persons interested therein can be required or are accustomed to
-- src:22498 | exercise their rights in accordance with the person’s instructions.
@ref s 244(2) (src:22492-22498)
GIVEN `the person has a right to acquire or dispose of the share or debenture or any interest in it, or to vote in respect of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's consent is necessary for the exercise of any of the rights of other persons interested in the share or debenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `other persons interested in the share or debenture can be required or are accustomed to exercise their rights in accordance with the person's instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(2) the person is deemed to have an interest in the share or debenture for the purposes of section 244` MEANS
    IF `the person has a right to acquire or dispose of the share or debenture or any interest in it, or to vote in respect of it` OR `the person's consent is necessary for the exercise of any of the rights of other persons interested in the share or debenture` OR `other persons interested in the share or debenture can be required or are accustomed to exercise their rights in accordance with the person's instructions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person is deemed to have an interest ... if" one of three; a deeming says who is treated as interested and does not say that no one else is

-- src:22500 | (3) Any person who fails to give any information required of the
-- src:22501 | person under this section, or who in giving any such information
-- src:22502 | makes any statement which the person knows to be false in a material
-- src:22503 | particular, or recklessly makes any statement which is false in a
-- src:22504 | material particular, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:22505 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:22506 | term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 244(3) (src:22500-22506)
GIVEN `the person fails to give information required of the person under section 244` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in giving the information the person makes a statement which the person knows to be false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in giving the information the person recklessly makes a statement which is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(3) the person is guilty of the offence of failing to give information or giving false information` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to give information required of the person under section 244` OR `in giving the information the person makes a statement which the person knows to be false in a material particular` OR `in giving the information the person recklessly makes a statement which is false in a material particular`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an element of the offence is unmet ("Any person who fails to give any information required ..., or who ... makes any statement which the person knows to be false in a material particular, or recklessly makes any statement which is false in a material particular, shall be guilty of an offence"); split site (i); fork F-K10

@ref s 244(3) (src:22500-22506)
GIVEN `the person fails to give information required of the person under section 244` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in giving the information the person makes a statement which the person knows to be false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in giving the information the person recklessly makes a statement which is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 244(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to give information required of the person under section 244` OR `in giving the information the person makes a statement which the person knows to be false in a material particular` OR `in giving the information the person recklessly makes a statement which is false in a material particular`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 12, TRUE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both"; no default penalty
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is fixed only for a person the subsection makes guilty

-- The duty to give the information has no time limit, so no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path); the false statement is a prohibition, and the act is the breach.
@ref s 244(3) (src:22500-22506)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 244(3) a person must give the information required of the person under section 244` MEANS   -- fork F-K34: a duty derived from the offence of failing to give information (s 244(3)); the text names the bearer ("Any person who fails to give any information required of the person")
    PARTY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person`
    MUST `s 244(3) give the Minister information required under section 244`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 244(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person did not give the information required of the person under section 244" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

@ref s 244(3) (src:22500-22506)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 244(3) a person must not make a statement to the Minister that the person knows to be false in a material particular, or recklessly make one` MEANS   -- fork F-K34: a prohibition derived from the offence of s 244(3); the text names the bearer
    PARTY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 244(3) make to the Minister a statement the person knows to be false in a material particular, or recklessly makes a statement false in a material particular`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person made to the Minister a statement the person knew to be false in a material particular, or recklessly made a statement false in a material particular"

-- src:22508 | (4) This section applies to a banking corporation but nothing
-- src:22509 | therein requires, subject to the provisions of the Banking Act 1970,
-- src:22514 | disclosure by a banking corporation to the Minister of any
-- src:22515 | information as to the affairs of any of its customers other than the
-- src:22516 | corporation of which it is the banker.
@ref s 244(4) (src:22508-22516)
GIVEN `the person is a banking corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(4) section 244 applies to the banking corporation` MEANS
    IF `the person is a banking corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a banking corporation"; for any other person the section applies as it reads

@ref s 244(4) (src:22508-22516)
GIVEN `the person is a banking corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is as to the affairs of a customer of the banking corporation other than the corporation of which the banking corporation is the banker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Banking Act 1970 provides that the banking corporation must disclose the information to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(4) section 244 requires the banking corporation to disclose the information to the Minister` MEANS
    IF `the person is a banking corporation` AND `the information is as to the affairs of a customer of the banking corporation other than the corporation of which the banking corporation is the banker`
    THEN (IF `the Banking Act 1970 provides that the banking corporation must disclose the information to the Minister`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to the provisions of the Banking Act 1970", which is not a source; the answer under that Act is for it
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing therein requires ... disclosure by a banking corporation to the Minister of any information as to the affairs of any of its customers other than the corporation of which it is the banker"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection excludes only a banking corporation's information about its other customers; for any other information section 244(1) governs

-- src:22518 | (5) The Minister may by notification in the Gazette delegate his or
-- src:22519 | her powers under this section either generally or in any particular case
-- src:22520 | to a committee of an approved exchange that has been approved by
-- src:22521 | the Minister under any written law relating to the securities industry
-- src:22522 | or to any body, panel or committee that has been established to advise
-- src:22523 | the Minister on matters connected with the securities industry.
-- src:22525 | [4/2017]
@ref s 244(5) (src:22518-22525)
GIVEN `the delegate is a committee of an approved exchange that has been approved by the Minister under a written law relating to the securities industry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegate is a body, panel or committee that has been established to advise the Minister on matters connected with the securities industry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegation is by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(5) the Minister may delegate the powers under section 244 to the delegate` MEANS
    IF `the delegation is by notification in the Gazette` AND (`the delegate is a committee of an approved exchange that has been approved by the Minister under a written law relating to the securities industry` OR `the delegate is a body, panel or committee that has been established to advise the Minister on matters connected with the securities industry`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Minister "may by notification in the Gazette delegate ... either generally or in any particular case" to the two kinds of delegate the subsection names; it says nothing of any other delegate or means

-- src:22527 | (6) A committee of an approved exchange or any body, panel or
-- src:22528 | committee mentioned in subsection (5) in the discharge of its powers
-- src:22529 | under that subsection must keep the Minister informed of any
-- src:22530 | information obtained under this section.
-- src:22532 | [4/2017]
@ref s 244(6) (src:22527-22532)
GIVEN `the person is a committee or body mentioned in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the committee or body is discharging its powers under that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(6) the committee or body must keep the Minister informed of any information obtained under section 244` MEANS
    IF `the person is a committee or body mentioned in subsection (5)` AND `the committee or body is discharging its powers under that subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty is stated for a committee or body "in the discharge of its powers under that subsection"; a gate of the "when" kind unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)

-- src:22534 | (7) Despite any delegation of the Minister’s powers under this
-- src:22535 | section, the Minister may exercise any of the powers conferred upon
-- src:22536 | the Minister under this section.
@ref s 244(7) (src:22534-22536)
GIVEN `the power is a power conferred upon the Minister under section 244` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(7) the Minister may exercise the power despite a delegation of it` MEANS
    IF `the power is a power conferred upon the Minister under section 244`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "any of the powers conferred upon the Minister under this section"

§ `Section 245: restrictions on shares or debentures`

DECLARE `s 245(1) act concerning the shares` IS ONE OF
    `s 245(1)(a) a transfer of the shares, an exercise of the right to acquire or dispose of the shares, or (for unissued shares) a transfer of the right to be issued with them or an issue of them`
    `s 245(1)(b) an exercise of voting rights in respect of the shares`
    `s 245(1)(c) an issue of further shares in right of the shares or pursuant to an offer made to the holder`
    `s 245(1)(d) a payment of sums due from the company on the shares, whether in respect of capital or otherwise`
    `s 245(1) any other act concerning the shares`

-- src:22540 | 245.—(1) Where in connection with an investigation under
-- src:22541 | section 243 or 244 it appears to the Minister that there is difficulty
-- src:22542 | in finding out the relevant facts about any shares, whether issued or to
-- src:22543 | be issued, the Minister may by order in the Gazette direct that the
-- src:22544 | shares are until further order subject to the following restrictions:
@ref s 245(1) (src:22540-22544)
GIVEN `in connection with an investigation under section 243 or 244 it appears to the Minister that there is difficulty in finding out the relevant facts about the shares, whether issued or to be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(1) the Minister may by order in the Gazette direct that the shares are until further order subject to the restrictions` MEANS
    IF `in connection with an investigation under section 243 or 244 it appears to the Minister that there is difficulty in finding out the relevant facts about the shares, whether issued or to be issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection begins "Where in connection with an investigation under section 243 or 244 it appears to the Minister that there is difficulty"; a "may" gated by "where" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-K7)

-- src:22546 | (a) that any transfer of those shares or any exercise of the right
-- src:22547 | to acquire or dispose of those shares or in the case of
-- src:22548 | unissued shares any transfer of the right to be issued
-- src:22549 | therewith and any issue thereof, is void;
-- src:22551 | (b) that no voting rights are exercisable in respect of those
-- src:22552 | shares;
-- src:22554 | (c) that no further shares may be issued in right of those shares
-- src:22555 | or pursuant to any offer made to the holder thereof; and
-- src:22557 | (d) that, except in a liquidation, no payment may be made of
-- src:22558 | any sums due from the company on those shares, whether
-- src:22559 | in respect of capital or otherwise.
@ref s 245(1)(a) to (d) (src:22546-22559)
GIVEN `the shares are subject to the restrictions by an order of the Minister under subsection (1) that has not been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act` IS A `s 245(1) act concerning the shares`
      `the company is in liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(1) the act is void or barred by the restrictions` MEANS
    IF NOT `the shares are subject to the restrictions by an order of the Minister under subsection (1) that has not been revoked`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restrictions are those to which the shares are "until further order subject" under an order of the Minister; with no such order the subsection says nothing
    ELSE CONSIDER `the act`
         WHEN `s 245(1)(a) a transfer of the shares, an exercise of the right to acquire or dispose of the shares, or (for unissued shares) a transfer of the right to be issued with them or an issue of them` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a) "is void"
         WHEN `s 245(1)(b) an exercise of voting rights in respect of the shares` THEN JUST TRUE                                                                                                          -- (b) "no voting rights are exercisable"
         WHEN `s 245(1)(c) an issue of further shares in right of the shares or pursuant to an offer made to the holder` THEN JUST TRUE                                                                    -- (c) "no further shares may be issued"
         WHEN `s 245(1)(d) a payment of sums due from the company on the shares, whether in respect of capital or otherwise` THEN
              (IF `the company is in liquidation`
               THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that, except in a liquidation, no payment may be made of any sums due from the company on those shares"
               ELSE JUST TRUE)
         WHEN `s 245(1) any other act concerning the shares` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a closed list: the shares are subject to "the following restrictions" (a) to (d) (fork F-K30)

-- src:22564 | (2) Any order of the Minister directing that shares will cease to be
-- src:22565 | subject to the restrictions mentioned in subsection (1) which is
-- src:22566 | expressed to be made with a view to permitting a transfer of those
-- src:22567 | shares may continue the application of subsection (1)(c) and (d), in
-- src:22568 | relation to those shares, either in whole or in part, so far as those
-- src:22569 | paragraphs relate to any right acquired or offer made before the
-- src:22570 | transfer.
@ref s 245(2) (src:22564-22570)
GIVEN `the order directs that the shares cease to be subject to the restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is expressed to be made with a view to permitting a transfer of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right was acquired or the offer made before the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(2) the order may continue the application of subsection (1)(c) and (d) to the shares` MEANS
    IF `the order directs that the shares cease to be subject to the restrictions` AND `the order is expressed to be made with a view to permitting a transfer of the shares` AND `the right was acquired or the offer made before the transfer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any order ... directing that shares will cease to be subject to the restrictions ... which is expressed to be made with a view to permitting a transfer ... may continue the application of subsection (1)(c) and (d) ... so far as those paragraphs relate to any right acquired or offer made before the transfer"

-- src:22572 | (3) Where any shares are for the time being subject to any
-- src:22573 | restrictions mentioned in subsection (1), any person who —
-- src:22575 | (a) having knowledge that the shares are subject to any such
-- src:22576 | restrictions, exercises or purports to exercise any right to
-- src:22577 | dispose of those shares, or of any right to be issued with the
-- src:22578 | shares;
-- src:22580 | (b) votes in respect of those shares, whether as holder or proxy,
-- src:22581 | or appoints a proxy to vote in respect thereof; or
-- src:22583 | (c) being the holder of any of those shares, fails to notify the
-- src:22584 | fact of their being subject to those restrictions to any
-- src:22585 | person whom the firstmentioned person does not know to
-- src:22586 | be aware of that fact but does know to be entitled, apart
-- src:22587 | from those restrictions, to vote in respect of those shares
-- src:22588 | whether as holder or proxy,
-- src:22590 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:22591 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:22592 | 12 months or to both.
@ref s 245(3) (src:22572-22592)
GIVEN `the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has knowledge that the shares are subject to the restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exercises or purports to exercise a right to dispose of the shares or a right to be issued with them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person votes in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy, or appoints a proxy to vote in respect of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the holder of some of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to notify the fact of their being subject to the restrictions to a person whom the person does not know to be aware of that fact but does know to be entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(3) the person is guilty of the offence of dealing in shares subject to the restrictions` MEANS
    IF `the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions mentioned in subsection (1)`
       AND (   (`the person has knowledge that the shares are subject to the restrictions` AND `the person exercises or purports to exercise a right to dispose of the shares or a right to be issued with them`)   -- (a)
            OR `the person votes in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy, or appoints a proxy to vote in respect of them`                                                                                 -- (b)
            OR (`the person is the holder of some of the shares` AND `the person fails to notify the fact of their being subject to the restrictions to a person whom the person does not know to be aware of that fact but does know to be entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy`))   -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an element of the offence is unmet ("Where any shares are for the time being subject to any restrictions ..., any person who — (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ... shall be guilty of an offence"); split site (i); fork F-K10

@ref s 245(3) (src:22572-22592)
GIVEN `the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has knowledge that the shares are subject to the restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exercises or purports to exercise a right to dispose of the shares or a right to be issued with them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person votes in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy, or appoints a proxy to vote in respect of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the holder of some of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to notify the fact of their being subject to the restrictions to a person whom the person does not know to be aware of that fact but does know to be entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 245(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions mentioned in subsection (1)`
       AND (   (`the person has knowledge that the shares are subject to the restrictions` AND `the person exercises or purports to exercise a right to dispose of the shares or a right to be issued with them`)
            OR `the person votes in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy, or appoints a proxy to vote in respect of them`
            OR (`the person is the holder of some of the shares` AND `the person fails to notify the fact of their being subject to the restrictions to a person whom the person does not know to be aware of that fact but does know to be entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of the shares, whether as holder or proxy`))
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 12, TRUE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both"; no default penalty
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is fixed only for a person the subsection makes guilty

@ref s 245(3)(a) (src:22575-22578)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 245(3)(a) a person must not exercise a right to dispose of shares subject to the restrictions, or a right to be issued with them, knowing of the restrictions` MEANS   -- fork F-K34: a prohibition derived from the offence of s 245(3); the text names the bearer ("any person who")
    PARTY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 245(3) exercise or purport to exercise a right to dispose of shares, or a right to be issued with shares, knowing they are subject to the restrictions`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person, knowing that the shares were subject to the restrictions, exercised or purported to exercise a right to dispose of them or a right to be issued with them"

@ref s 245(3)(b) (src:22580-22581)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 245(3)(b) a person must not vote in respect of shares subject to the restrictions or appoint a proxy to vote` MEANS   -- fork F-K34: a prohibition derived from the offence of s 245(3); the text names the bearer ("any person who")
    PARTY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 245(3) vote in respect of shares subject to the restrictions, or appoint a proxy to vote`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person voted in respect of shares subject to the restrictions, or appointed a proxy to vote in respect of them"

-- (c) is a duty to notify with no time limit, so no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 245(3)(c) (src:22583-22588)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 245(3)(c) the holder must notify the persons entitled to vote of the restrictions` MEANS   -- fork F-K34: a duty derived from the offence of failing to notify (s 245(3)(c)); the text names the bearer ("being the holder of any of those shares")
    PARTY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person`
    MUST `s 245(3) notify the holders entitled to vote of the restrictions`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 245(3)(c) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a person` `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the holder did not notify a person entitled to vote that the shares were subject to the restrictions" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:22594 | (4) Where shares in any company are issued in contravention of the
-- src:22595 | restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1), the company and
-- src:22596 | every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an
-- src:22597 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:22598 | $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months.
@ref s 245(4) (src:22594-22598)
GIVEN `shares in the company have been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(4) the officer is guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions` MEANS
    IF `shares in the company have been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1)` AND `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an element of the offence is unmet ("Where shares in any company are issued in contravention of the restrictions ..., the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence"); split site (i); fork F-K10; "officer in default" is an input (the keel's s 408(3) seam)

@ref s 245(4) (src:22594-22598)
GIVEN `shares in the company have been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(4) the company is guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions` MEANS
    IF `shares in the company have been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an element of the offence is unmet ("Where shares in any company are issued in contravention of the restrictions ..., the company ... shall be guilty of an offence"); split site (i); fork F-K10

@ref s 245(4) (src:22594-22598)
GIVEN `shares in the company have been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 245(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `shares in the company have been issued in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 12, FALSE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months": "or", so not both; the one sentence is stated for the company and for the officer
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is fixed only for the company and the officer the subsection makes guilty

@ref s 245(4) (src:22594-22598)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 245(4) the company must not issue shares in contravention of the restrictions` MEANS   -- fork F-K34: a prohibition derived from the offence of s 245(4); the text names the bearer ("the company and every officer of the company who is in default")
    PARTY `s 231 a company` `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 245(4) issue shares in contravention of the restrictions`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 a company` `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company issued shares in contravention of the restrictions imposed pursuant to section 245(1)"

-- src:22600 | (5) A prosecution must not be instituted under this section except
-- src:22601 | with the consent of the Public Prosecutor.
@ref s 245(5) (src:22600-22601)
GIVEN `the prosecution is a prosecution under section 245` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(5) the prosecution is barred for want of the consent of the Public Prosecutor` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prosecution is a prosecution under section 245`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "A prosecution ... under this section"
    ELSE (IF `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the prosecution`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be instituted under this section except with the consent of the Public Prosecutor"; an "except" met
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:22603 | (6) This section applies in relation to debentures as it applies in
-- src:22604 | relation to shares.
@ref s 245(6) (src:22603-22604)
GIVEN `the restrictions are imposed on debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(6) section 245 applies to the debentures as it applies to shares` MEANS
    IF `the restrictions are imposed on debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "debentures"

§ `Section 246: inspectors appointed in other countries`

-- src:22611 | 246. Where —
-- src:22613 | (a) under a corresponding law of another country an inspector
-- src:22614 | has been appointed to investigate the affairs of a
-- src:22615 | corporation; and
-- src:22617 | (b) the Minister is of the opinion that, in connection with that
-- src:22618 | investigation, it is expedient that an investigation be made
-- src:22619 | in Singapore,
-- src:22621 | the Minister may by notice declare that the inspector so appointed is
-- src:22622 | to have the same powers and duties in Singapore in relation to the
-- src:22623 | investigation as if the corporation were a declared company and the
-- src:22624 | inspector had been appointed under section 231 and thereupon the
-- src:22625 | inspector has those powers and duties.
@ref s 246 (src:22611-22625)
GIVEN `under a corresponding law of another country an inspector has been appointed to investigate the affairs of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is of the opinion that, in connection with that investigation, it is expedient that an investigation be made in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 246 the Minister may by notice declare that the inspector is to have the same powers and duties in Singapore as an inspector appointed under section 231` MEANS
    IF `under a corresponding law of another country an inspector has been appointed to investigate the affairs of a corporation` AND `the Minister is of the opinion that, in connection with that investigation, it is expedient that an investigation be made in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section begins "Where — (a) under a corresponding law ... an inspector has been appointed ...; and (b) the Minister is of the opinion that ... it is expedient"; a "may" gated by "where" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-K7)

@ref s 246 (src:22611-22625)
GIVEN `the Minister has by notice declared that the inspector is to have the same powers and duties in Singapore as if the corporation were a declared company and the inspector had been appointed under section 231` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 246 the inspector has the powers and duties of an inspector appointed under section 231` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has by notice declared that the inspector is to have the same powers and duties in Singapore as if the corporation were a declared company and the inspector had been appointed under section 231`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the inspector has those powers and duties "thereupon", on the Minister's declaration; a "thereupon" unmet (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))
